# This source tree is CP1252, not UTF-8, and line endings are mixed both
# across and within files (some files carry CRLF on older lines and LF on
# more recent ones). This is the historical, working state of the code and
# is left as-is deliberately: it is not an oversight to "fix".
#
# The display-string tables (src/text_*.inc) rely on their exact CP1252 byte
# values to index into the generated font tables (src/Fonts/*.inc). Any
# re-encoding to UTF-8 or line-ending normalisation would corrupt those
# tables and silently change what the device renders on screen. This
# repository also mirrors an upstream master, so any byte drift here would
# create needless merge conflicts on every sync.
#
# `-text` tells Git to leave these files alone: no line-ending conversion,
# no encoding conversion, on checkout or checkin.
*.asm -text
*.inc -text
*.INC -text
*.lkr -text
